---
import Layout from "../layout/Layout.astro";
import "../style/pages/legal.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | ToolVector"
  description="Learn how ToolVector collects, uses, and protects your information when you use our software review and comparison platform."
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-page__hero">
      <div class="container legal-page__hero-inner">
        <div class="legal-page__badge">Legal</div>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-page__meta">
          Last updated: <time datetime="2026-07-29">July 29, 2026</time>
        </p>
        <p class="legal-page__lead">
          This Privacy Policy explains how ToolVector collects, uses, shares,
          and protects your information when you access or use our software
          review and comparison platform.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container legal-page__body">
      <aside class="legal-toc">
        <p class="legal-toc__label">On this page</p>
        <nav>
          <a href="#introduction">1. Introduction</a>
          <a href="#information-we-collect">2. Information We Collect</a>
          <a href="#how-we-use">3. How We Use Your Information</a>
          <a href="#cookies">4. Cookies &amp; Tracking</a>
          <a href="#sharing">5. Sharing Your Information</a>
          <a href="#your-rights">6. Your Rights</a>
          <a href="#data-security">7. Data Security</a>
          <a href="#data-retention">8. Data Retention</a>
          <a href="#childrens-privacy">9. Children's Privacy</a>
          <a href="#changes">10. Changes to This Policy</a>
          <a href="#contact">11. Contact Us</a>
        </nav>
      </aside>

      <article class="legal-content">
        <div class="legal-notice">
          <span class="legal-notice__icon">⚠️</span>
          <p>
            This is a suggested draft/outline based on currently visible site
            features. This is not legal advice. Have a lawyer review it before
            publishing — especially if you have users in the EU (GDPR),
            California (CCPA), or other regions with specific data protection
            laws.
          </p>
        </div>

        <section id="introduction">
          <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
          <p>
            ToolVector ("we," "us," "the site") operates <strong
              >toolvector.io</strong
            > — a software review and comparison platform. This Privacy Policy explains
            how we collect, use, share, and protect your information when you access
            or use our services.
          </p>
          <p>
            By using ToolVector, you agree to the terms described in this
            Policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="information-we-collect">
          <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

          <h3>a) Information you provide directly</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Email address when you subscribe to our weekly software digest
            </li>
            <li>Account information when you sign in / register</li>
            <li>
              Answers submitted through the <strong>Smart Match</strong> tool (team
              goals, company size, industry, etc.) used to generate a personalized
              shortlist of tools
            </li>
            <li>
              Information submitted via the <strong>"List your tool"</strong> form
              (for software vendors): company name, product description, contact details
            </li>
            <li>
              Content you submit through contact forms, comments, or review
              feedback
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h3>b) Information collected automatically</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>IP address, browser type, device, operating system</li>
            <li>Pages viewed, time spent, referral source</li>
            <li>
              Cookies and similar tracking technologies (see <a href="#cookies"
                >Section 4</a
              >)
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h3>c) Information from third parties</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Data from affiliate partners (e.g., when you click on deals for
              Semrush, NordVPN, Notion, etc.) used to track referrals
            </li>
            <li>
              If you sign in via Google or another social provider: name, email,
              and public profile photo (if this feature is enabled)
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="how-we-use">
          <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
          <p>We use your information to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Provide Smart Match results and personalized software
              recommendations
            </li>
            <li>
              Send newsletters, new review updates, and deal notifications (if
              you've subscribed)
            </li>
            <li>Operate and improve the website, and analyze user behavior</li>
            <li>Process vendor submissions from the "List your tool" form</li>
            <li>
              Measure the performance of affiliate links and advertising
              programs
            </li>
            <li>Prevent fraud and ensure system security</li>
            <li>Comply with legal obligations where required</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="cookies">
          <h2>4. Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</h2>
          <p>ToolVector uses cookies and similar technologies to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Remember your preferences (e.g., saved Smart Match results)</li>
            <li>
              Analyze site traffic (e.g., via Google Analytics or a similar
              tool)
            </li>
            <li>
              Track affiliate links to accurately attribute referral commissions
            </li>
            <li>Show relevant ads/deals (if applicable)</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            You can disable cookies in your browser settings, though some
            features (like saved shortlists) may not work properly as a result.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="sharing">
          <h2>5. Sharing Your Information</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong> We may share
            information with:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Service providers</strong> (hosting, email marketing, analytics)
              needed to operate the site
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Affiliate/advertising partners</strong>, limited to what's
              necessary to track referrals (typically anonymized data or click
              IDs, not direct personal information)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Law enforcement or regulators</strong> when legally required
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a> page
            for more details on our commission model.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="your-rights">
          <h2>6. Your Rights</h2>
          <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Access, correct, or delete your personal information</li>
            <li>
              Withdraw consent (e.g., unsubscribe from the newsletter at any
              time via the "unsubscribe" link)
            </li>
            <li>Request a copy of your data (EU users under GDPR)</li>
            <li>
              Opt out of certain data processing (California residents under
              CCPA)
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            To exercise these rights, contact us at:
            <a href="mailto:yen@toolvector.io"
              >yen@toolvector.io</a
            >
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="data-security">
          <h2>7. Data Security</h2>
          <p>
            We apply reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect
            your information from unauthorized access, use, or disclosure.
            However, no method of transmission over the Internet is 100% secure.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="data-retention">
          <h2>8. Data Retention</h2>
          <p>
            We retain personal information only for as long as necessary to
            fulfill the purposes described in this Policy, or as required by
            law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="childrens-privacy">
          <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            ToolVector is not directed at individuals under 16 years of age, and
            we do not knowingly collect information from children. If we become
            aware of such a case, we will delete the relevant information
            promptly.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="changes">
          <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Last
            updated" date at the top of this page will reflect the most recent
            changes. We encourage you to review this page periodically.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="contact">
          <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us:
          </p>
          <div class="legal-contact-card">
            <a href="mailto:yen@toolvector.io">
              <span>📧</span> yen@toolvector.io
            </a>
            <a href="/contact/">
              <span>🌐</span> toolvector.io/contact
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="legal-footer-note">
          This Privacy Policy should be read together with our
          <a href="/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a> and
          <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
